 a graze. Stay near a live hitbox to keep earning TP continuously: Seth gains 6 TP per second of grazing; Aqua gains 60. Normal page damage is 2 (READ / counter 3); timed Notebook damage is 2–6. Paid specials unleash much denser attacks. Aqua spends 4–15 TP on ordinary patterns, 35 on the finale. RECOVER costs 35 TP for stamina; SECOND WIND costs 45 for a full refill; MEND costs 30 for 16 HP. EDGE GUARD costs 15, CROSSCUT 25. Recovery spends TP and her attack turn. Frustration makes her attack faster and can buy a warned pattern change or Cyan turn. When hurt, she may dodge carefully and save 100 TP for STILL WATERS, a 24-second attack. Her final barrage sends large knives beyond the box during Yellow: the diagonal dance lane stays open. Opposing knife walls share an opening before it moves. Both 100-TP attacks keep the current chapter. Only after all ten healing items are used, reaching 18 HP makes Aqua prepare her finale for a later paid turn; she gains no free health or stamina. During either human’s attack, a hit leaving Aqua at 12 HP or less forces her SOUL back into her body and ends the attack early. Timed Notebook hits, ordinary throws and every TP skill use the same recall. She survives lethal hits until the finale has ended. Damage and resources carry over; there is no free heal, TP refund or attack retry. Even an otherwise lethal counter forces this withdrawal with 1 HP left. Breaking the finale opens the finishing turn. Below half health she dodges more cautiously and telegraphs local knife cuts; cuts share her three-parry limit and spend stamina. Healing costs her resources and her attack opportunity. Surviving her full barrage still opens a finishing turn. Knife tells: leave the cyan path before her full-stage lunge; the red arc marks the ending cut. Mid-attack CYAN TURN warns before she changes her own soul and rotates the stage; BIND prevents it. Later combinations warn again for a second cut. A purple ring and Z mark her recovery: throw now for a stronger counter. BAIT lengthens that opening and prevents the second cut; BIND prevents lunges. Cyan: move around the orbit; Z reverses it. Aqua spins the box from outside. Green only: WASD controls your shield, arrow keys choose attacks at Aqua. On touch, use the D-pad to guard and tap UP / LEFT / DOWN / RIGHT in the arena to attack.</p><p>Original UNDERTALE fan battle. Aqua is a living human in this continuity. LV 10 against LV 14. Original artwork. Player supplied theme: Mary had a little lamb but it's a boss theme.<br><a href="https://fontstruct.com/fontstructions/show/2368299">Determination</a> by anonymous-1438277 · <a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="Determination-license.txt">CC BY 3.0</a><br>Knife fan, chain, and orbit patterns inspired by Aqua in DELTARUNE.</p></details></dialog><div id="live" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><script>(async()=>{const modules=Object.create(null),cache=Object.create(null);function require(id){if(cache[id])return cache[id];const exports=cache[id]={};modules[id](exports,require);return exports;}
